IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 7183 of 2021
CITATION: (2006) 4 SCC 1
YEAR: 2006

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Y.K. Sabharwal, Arun Kumar, G.P. Mathur, C.K. Thakker, P.K. Balasubramanyan

PARTIES:
State of Karnataka vs Umadevi

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Constitution of India

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Article 14, Article 16, Article 309

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
regularization of back door appointments, ad-hoc employees, constitutional public employment

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Constitution bench held that courts cannot direct absorption or regularization of temporary or ad-hoc public workers appointed without sanctioned recruitment process.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Article 14, Article 16, Article 309.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

